# Notarization credentials for `scripts/build-signed.sh`.
#
# Copy to `.env.signing` (gitignored) and fill in ONE of the two methods below.
# The signing identity itself is auto-discovered from your keychain — you do NOT
# put it here. With no file present the build is signed but not notarized.

# ── Method A: App Store Connect API key (recommended) ──────────────────────
# Non-expiring, revocable, and the only method that works in CI. Create a key at
# https://appstoreconnect.apple.com/access/integrations/api (role: Developer),
# download the .p8 ONCE, and store it outside the repo.
#
# APPLE_API_ISSUER=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx   # Issuer ID (UUID)
# APPLE_API_KEY=XXXXXXXXXX                                # Key ID (10 chars)
# APPLE_API_KEY_PATH=/absolute/path/to/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8

# ── Method B: Apple ID + app-specific password ─────────────────────────────
# Quickest for a one-off local notarized build. Generate an app-specific
# password at https://account.apple.com → Sign-In and Security → App-Specific
# Passwords (this is NOT your Apple ID password).
#
# APPLE_ID=you@example.com
# APPLE_PASSWORD=abcd-efgh-ijkl-mnop        # app-specific password
# APPLE_TEAM_ID=72FBK9YTA3
